<InfoLayout title="Terms and Educational Limitations" description="Read the scope of this educational lab, its mathematical assumptions, synthetic-data labels, and limitations on interpreting probability as prediction." eyebrow="Understand the boundaries" lead="This lab explains a specified model. Its purpose is educational understanding, with clear limits on what the examples establish.">
  <h2>Educational scope</h2><p>WinGo Learning Lab provides articles, illustrations, and browser-based educational tools about classifications, probability, and randomness. It does not accept wagers, process financial transactions, or operate a prediction service. The homepage includes an optional, labeled referral link to external game registration. Demo-only access has not been verified; the external platform's terms and access requirements apply after you leave this site.</p><p>The project is independent. Use of a familiar game-format name describes the topic being studied and does not claim an official operator relationship.</p>
  <h2>Mathematical assumptions</h2><p>Unless an example explicitly says otherwise, the theoretical model uses independent draws from ten equally likely digits, 0 through 9. Size and color are assigned using the <a href="/wingo-rules/">selected example ruleset</a>.</p><p>A probability calculation is conditional on those assumptions. It does not establish the fairness, design, or outcome distribution of an external system. A past sequence alone cannot reliably forecast an independent random outcome.</p>
  <h2>Illustrations and tool status</h2><p>Constructed examples are labeled as illustrative. They are not live results or evidence of an external game history. The simulator and randomness tools generate outcomes locally. The calculator computes probabilities under the stated model and can compare them with a local sample. Recorded replay restores a completed dataset without sampling again.</p><p>Local experiments describe the disclosed model. They are not future external outcomes or verified predictive signals. Reset or reload clears in-memory run history; user-initiated CSV export creates a local download.</p>
  <h2>No guaranteed result</h2><p>The material does not promise winnings, investment returns, predictive accuracy, or a successful strategy. A visually striking pattern can be described without supporting a claim about the next draw. Treat the worked examples as an opportunity to examine reasoning and assumptions.</p>
  <h2>Sources and corrections</h2><p>Guides cite references for substantive concepts and document the selected ruleset. Sources can change, and errors can occur. See the <a href="/contact/">contact information page</a> for the current public contact channel or its pending status.</p><p>The <a href="/about/">about page</a> explains the project, and the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy page</a> describes the implementation’s current data practices.</p>
</InfoLayout>
